        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="0" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="1" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

-Receptacles

-Some windows

-Both doors

-Furnace combustion air supply

-Hole in the floor in the mechanical room

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings. 

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the assessment, the insulation of the exterior walls was R-19. We recommend upgrading the insulation level. You are eligible for $2.50/square inch for the addition of R-20+,  and $ 3.50/square inch for R-30+. The insulation will help you to increase the airtightness of your home and contribute to energy savings.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the time of the audit, the attic insulation inspection was not possible. We estimated the insulation level to be R-40. We recommend the addition of insulation to reach R-60. </ceilings>
                <WaterConservation>At the time of the audit, we noticed one 13L toilet. We recommend the replacement of a low flow toilet. The replacement will help you to reduce water consumption.</WaterConservation>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
